{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3287","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3287","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3287\",\"parent_revision\":\"cbbf724f6303bbe9d9efc0a1b8143d380b72335af7b4afafcc75102d71be2d7f\",\"root_revision\":\"cbbf724f6303bbe9d9efc0a1b8143d380b72335af7b4afafcc75102d71be2d7f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-28/29 during `/dh:complete-implementation Pb31107bf`'s quality-gate loop for #3268. QG task T0 (Multi-Perspective Review, dispatched via `dh:task-worker` per the phase mapping table's \\\"(orchestrated)\\\" role) created plan `Pf807b3cf` (feature slug `review-3268-20260828T154026Z-9c942f5f8fb893c0`) and made real progress: T1 (Security) APPROVE, T2 (Performance) SKIP, T4 (Accessibility) SKIP all completed; only T5 (Synthesis, depends on T1-T4) remained, ready to dispatch.\\n\\nThe dispatching agent (`qgt0-3268`) then crashed mid-run due to an infrastructure rate-limit error (`idleReason: \\\"failed\\\"`, `failureReason: \\\"API Error: Server is temporarily limiting requests... Rate limited\\\"`) \u2014 confirmed via `sam_task(action='read')` on `Pdade66b4/T0`: still `in-progress`, claimed, never completed. Per `implement-feature/SKILL.md`'s Agent Health Check crash-recovery procedure, the task was re-spawned with the same task reference (`Pdade66b4/T0`).\\n\\nThe respawned agent (`qgt0-3268-resume`) did not detect or resume the existing 80%-complete `Pf807b3cf` plan. Instead it created an entirely new plan \u2014 `Pf0e2e907` (feature slug `review-3268-20260828T215919Z-199bbc9958939367`, confirmed via `sam_plan(action='list', search='review-3268')` showing both plans) \u2014 and re-dispatched all four reviewer perspectives (Security, Performance, Quality, Accessibility) from scratch, duplicating three already-complete reviews (Security, Performance, Accessibility) for the same changed-file set on the same issue (#3268).\\n\\nRoot cause not fully diagnosed, but the mechanism is visible: `dh:multi-perspective-review`'s plan-slug generation appears to be `review-{issue}-{timestamp}-{hash}` \u2014 a fresh timestamp on every invocation, with no step that first searches for an existing plan matching `review-{issue}-*` with incomplete tasks before creating a new one. SAM plans generally support a resume pattern (query `ready`, dispatch what's ready) \u2014 multi-perspective-review's own orchestration doesn't use it across separate invocations of the same T0 task.\\n\\nImpact: any crash-and-respawn of a QG T0 task (or any other trigger that re-invokes multi-perspective-review for the same issue mid-flight) re-runs completed reviewer work at full cost, potentially multiple times. No incorrect verdicts resulted this time (verdicts should be substantively repeatable for the same diff), but the compute/token cost is pure duplication.\\n\\nUser-provided context: none \u2014 whether the fix is a plan-lookup-and-resume step at the start of multi-perspective-review's orchestration, a deterministic (non-timestamped) plan slug keyed only on issue number, or something else is a design question for grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 development-harness /dh:complete-implementation for #3268, QG plan Pdade66b4\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d7dd2b2a2bad208e0eb6846288d96dfb295cbda351085a91ffcf162b0d7c302a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5sgg\"}"}